/*
  The career corpus the conversational agent answers from.

  97 careers and 51 government-job routes, extracted from
  career-intelligence.html — the same records the page renders, including
  the RIASEC theme codes each career is already tagged with. That tagging
  is the bridge between a client's saved profile and this corpus, and it
  is why an answer here can be about them rather than about careers in
  general.

  ── Why this is a file and not a prompt ──

  The whole corpus is about 115 KB, which is far too much to send with
  every message. What the agent gets in its cached system prompt is
  catalogue() — id, title, sector and themes only, a few thousand tokens —
  so it knows what exists and can name a real id. Full records come back
  one at a time through the lookup_career tool.

  ── Why the agent may only quote from here ──

  A student can already ask any model what a data scientist earns. The
  reason to ask ours is that ours answers from figures a counsellor
  reviewed, in rupees, against Indian entrance exams. Nothing in the
  agent's instructions permits it to describe a career that is not in
  this file, and searchCareers() returning nothing is a real answer the
  agent has to relay rather than route around.

  Regenerate rather than hand-edit if career-intelligence.html changes.
*/

